== Trivia ==
* {{dlc|nr}} Although the D6 is considered a [[Special Item]], it will only count as a special item if found naturally during gameplay. Starting with the D6 as {{c|Isaac}} will not cause fewer special items to appear later on. This fact also extends to {{c|Eden}}'s starting items: if Eden starts with a special item, that item will not count toward the special item total.
* In the original ''Binding of Isaac'', the D6 had a recharge time of 3 instead of 6.
** The D6 could not reroll special boss items in the original game, such as {{i|Little C.H.A.D.}} and {{i|Little Steven}}.
* In the Eternal Edition of the original ''Binding of Isaac'', The D6 has a chance to delete the item instead of rerolling it when playing in hard mode.
** {{dlc|r}} The {{i|Eternal D6|n}} has the same effect but with a 2 room charge.
* In the original Binding of Isaac, this item was called "The Dice".
** Like the other dice items, the D6 uses the naming scheme of dice for tabletop RPGs like ''Dungeons & Dragons,'' which were associated with devil worship during the Satanic Panic.
* The {{i|D7}}, {{i|D8}}, {{i|D12}}, {{i|D20}}, {{i|D100}}, {{i|Spindown Dice}}, and {{i|D infinity}} has the sides displayed with numbers, while {{i|D1}}, {{i|D4}}, {{i|The D6}}, and the {{i|Eternal D6}} has sides displayed with pips.
* The D6 is the only dice item that includes ‘The’ in its name.
** This may be because it is ‘The’ quintessential dice item; being the first added to the game, arguably the most iconic, and the only one featured as a starting item - for Isaac himself, no less.

